# The Claude models production runs, per role.
#
#   main <model-id>    CLAUDE_MODEL — SQL generation (Ask AI), dashboards,
#                      subject design, investigations, schema profiling
#   light <model-id>   CLAUDE_MODEL_HAIKU — answer formatting, result checks,
#                      morning briefs, KPI drafts, query starters
#
# Editing this file on main runs .github/workflows/claude-model.yml, which
# sets both variables on the backend (new revision, Provisioned, 100%
# traffic) and on the jobs-worker (restart). No-op when the values already
# match — NOT a promote vehicle. A per-category override on /admin/ai-usage
# still wins over these for the categories it names.
#
# ROLLBACK: set `main claude-sonnet-4-6` and push. The request shaping in
# backend/src/ai/modelCapabilities.ts serves both generations, so either
# value is safe with the code that ships alongside this file. It is NOT safe
# with code older than that: Sonnet 5 refuses the fixed thinking budget and
# `temperature` the older code sent — which is why the workflow refuses to
# apply while the Build & Deploy run for its own commit failed.
#
# 2026-09-24: Sonnet 4.6 → Sonnet 5 (owner: "Yes do it"). Sonnet 5 is the
# successor at $2/$10 per MTok vs $3/$15, with a tokenizer that counts ~30%
# more tokens for the same text — so ~13% cheaper like for like, and the
# point of the move is quality, not price. Haiku 4.5 has no successor.
